/home/agentops/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/docs/extension-api.md:- The owning Pi session is the only publisher for its own pane metadata. When an active workflow has an explicit bounded `label`, the newest active label appears in the summary and compact `title-suffix`; overlapping completion restores the previous active label. Raw task and goal prompts never enter Herdr metadata. Without a label, one active run uses its agent name and two or more use the active-run count. Attention adds `⚠`, and the suffix is cleared when active work reaches zero.
/home/agentops/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/docs/extension-api.md:For substantial work in another codebase, Herdr 0.7.5+ can open a project-owned Pi pane rooted in that repository:
